+// authoring is LINEAR in the angle, so the azimuth is the authored number
+// exactly -- there is nothing to invert.
+//
+// ELEVATION IS NOT. Vertically MK64 does not author an angle at all: it
+// places a PIXEL ROW in the screen its own perspective camera rasterises
+// into, so the angle is whatever that camera's projection makes of the row,
+// and recovering it is an inversion of guPerspective and nothing more:
+//   ndc_y(ob) = 1 - 2*ob/240        (MEASURED -- see below)
